Problem Statement
A campus parking office manages vehicle parking slots.
Each vehicle record is stored using the vehicle number as the key, and the corresponding value is a dictionary containing:
• Owner
• Slot
• Status
The system should support adding vehicles, updating parking slots, fetching vehicle details, and listing vehicles parked in a particular zone.
Class Creation
class ParkingLotSystem:
 
Constructor
def __init__(self):
   self.vehicles = {}
 
Operations
1. Add Vehicle
Function Prototype
def add_vehicle(self, vehicle_no: str, owner: str, slot: str) -> dict:
 
Example Input
system.add_vehicle("KA22MN4501", "Dev", "C-18")
 
Expected Output
{
   "KA22MN4501": {
       "owner": "Dev",
       "slot": "C-18",
       "status": "Parked"
   }
}
 
Implementation Flow
• Check whether vehicle_no already exists in self.vehicles.
• If the vehicle already exists, raise:
ValueError("Vehicle already exists")
 
• Otherwise, add a nested dictionary containing:
• owner
• slot
• status as "Parked"
• Return self.vehicles.
Hidden Test Focus
Duplicate vehicle numbers must raise only:
ValueError("Vehicle already exists")
 
2. Update Slot
Function Prototype
def update_slot(self, vehicle_no: str, new_slot: str) -> dict:
 
Example Input
system.update_slot("KA22MN4501", "C-22")
 
Expected Output
{
   "KA22MN4501": {
       "owner": "Dev",
       "slot": "C-22",
       "status": "Parked"
   }
}
 
Implementation Flow
• Check whether vehicle_no exists in self.vehicles.
• If the vehicle does not exist, raise:
KeyError("Vehicle not found")
 
• Update only the slot value.
• Do not modify owner or status.
• Return self.vehicles.
Hidden Test Focus
Updating a missing vehicle must raise only:
KeyError("Vehicle not found")
 
